                        "sense_id": "f67d94d9-f413-30bc-9548-9a0daaec8a55",
                        "entry_id": "8f3692f3-cf0b-3265-a482-ee2cfc05597b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A plant that is grown alongside a crop in order to improve its growth; A companion crop."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b01fbf7-8cf1-4ac7-b882-f1e5d1003c21",
                                "sense_id": "f67d94d9-f413-30bc-9548-9a0daaec8a55",
                                "text": "The annual and perennial lupine and sweet clover may be regarded as the best siderates."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce47a91b-b718-4037-8314-989440babfce",
                                "sense_id": "f67d94d9-f413-30bc-9548-9a0daaec8a55",
                                "text": "New types of mineral fertilizers, higher quality organic matter, and other biological means of compensating for the lost nutrients (including siderates) can reduce the required amounts of mineral fertilizers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e03f3bd1-424c-4730-9c74-b307ca888f9a",
                                "sense_id": "f67d94d9-f413-30bc-9548-9a0daaec8a55",
                                "text": "In such situation, environment-forming possibilities of crop rotations (including perennial legume herbs, siderates, after-harvest cultures, etc.) and different soil cultivation techniques (which may either attenuate or on the contrary to significantly increase the variegation of fields) play a peculiar role in the SAR \"formation\"."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
