                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f995289-aa39-37aa-a281-e906bcecabd0",
                        "entry_id": "1f019f06-b924-33e4-9a22-93c284c3a541",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To strike down or incapacitate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbac5aee-5ff1-4f79-9a09-0b989362f21c",
                                "sense_id": "2f995289-aa39-37aa-a281-e906bcecabd0",
                                "text": "When it is impossible to use the protoxide either alone or according to the method of M. Bert, recourse may be had to the mixed method, which consists in siderating the patient with the protoxide and continuing the anesthesia with ether or chloroform."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1335735f-aeb1-49e5-bab4-5d301d9db0ad",
                                "sense_id": "2f995289-aa39-37aa-a281-e906bcecabd0",
                                "text": "This is done in order to put the horse in a state of action inhibition (i.e. siderating the animal) before putting the saddle on and mounting."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2a53728-bc83-48f7-9969-6b2408b75d3a",
                                "sense_id": "2f995289-aa39-37aa-a281-e906bcecabd0",
                                "text": "Besides intercourse (when the Image-repertoire goes to the devil), there is that other embrace, which is a motionless cradling: we are enchanged, bewitched: we are in the realm of sleep, without sleeping; we are within the voluptuous infantilism of sleepiness: this is the moment for telling stories, the moment of the voice which takes me, siderates [i.e. strikes] me, this is the return to the mother ('in the loving calm of your arms,' says a poem set to music by Duparc)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
